{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"cart_ox","model_identifier":"cart_ox","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"## cart_ox\n\nOx cart (E5).\n\n- Cubes: 67 (18 rotated). Texture 256x256, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -24.0..24.0, y -0.0..46.4, z -131.3..48.0 (size 48.0 x 46.4 x 179.3 u = 135 x 130 x 504 cm).\nOx cart: a four-wheeled farm wagon for one ox or horse. Body 3 m long (96 u bed + wheels = 92 u axle-to-axle span with wheels; 179 u including the shafts), 48 u wide, with low plank sides (20 cm), corner stakes, a driver's bench at the front, a hinged tailboard, iron-tyred four-spoke 0.8 m wheels on two axles, a team-colour stripe on both sides and a pair of shafts that rise to the animal's collar. Faces -Z.\n\n**Hit box:** body box 48 x 36 x 100 u from y = 0 centred x = 0, z = 0 (the shafts are not solid; the hauling animal has its own hit box).\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `body` (pivot on the axle line) > `shafts`, `tailboard` (hinge at the rear floor edge); `wheel_fr/fl/br/bl` on `root`.\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the shaft tips (45 u up, 131 u ahead of the origin), where they meet the animal's collar (an ox/horse stands between the shafts with its collar here); `slot_rider` on the driver's bench (hips at 36 u up); `slot_cargo` on the floor centre (D6 loads such as logs, sacks and stone sit here, their origin on the floor; lay several side by side); `slot_crew_1` / `slot_crew_2` walking beside (front-left, back-right).\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s, ox walk): one wheel turn per 2.47 s (circumference 88.0 u); the body bobs and rocks slightly.\n\n**Key times:** `use` (unload) 2.4 s: the tailboard drops open at 0.7 s (key: cargo comes off), closes by 2.4 s. `idle` still with a faint shaft creak. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder, the rear-right wheel wobbles. `destroyed` holds: both right wheels break off and fall flat, the body crashes onto its right side, the tailboard falls open and the shafts drop.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 2.471 | loop |\n| `use` | 2.4 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.8 | hold |\n"},"description":"## cart_ox\n\nOx cart (E5).\n\n- Cubes: 67 (18 rotated). Texture 256x256, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -24.0..24.0, y -0.0..46.4, z -131.3..48.0 (size 48.0 x 46.4 x 179.3 u = 135 x 130 x 504 cm).\nOx cart: a four-wheeled farm wagon for one ox or horse. Body 3 m long (96 u bed + wheels = 92 u axle-to-axle span with wheels; 179 u including the shafts), 48 u wide, with low plank sides (20 cm), corner stakes, a driver's bench at the front, a hinged tailboard, iron-tyred four-spoke 0.8 m wheels on two axles, a team-colour stripe on both sides and a pair of shafts that rise to the animal's collar. Faces -Z.\n\n**Hit box:** body box 48 x 36 x 100 u from y = 0 centred x = 0, z = 0 (the shafts are not solid; the hauling animal has its own hit box).\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `body` (pivot on the axle line) > `shafts`, `tailboard` (hinge at the rear floor edge); `wheel_fr/fl/br/bl` on `root`.\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the shaft tips (45 u up, 131 u ahead of the origin), where they meet the animal's collar (an ox/horse stands between the shafts with its collar here); `slot_rider` on the driver's bench (hips at 36 u up); `slot_cargo` on the floor centre (D6 loads such as logs, sacks and stone sit here, their origin on the floor; lay several side by side); `slot_crew_1` / `slot_crew_2` walking beside (front-left, back-right).\n\n**Move speed:** `move` designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s, ox walk): one wheel turn per 2.47 s (circumference 88.0 u); the body bobs and rocks slightly.\n\n**Key times:** `use` (unload) 2.4 s: the tailboard drops open at 0.7 s (key: cargo comes off), closes by 2.4 s. `idle` still with a faint shaft creak. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder, the rear-right wheel wobbles. `destroyed` holds: both right wheels break off and fall flat, the body crashes onto its right side, the tailboard falls open and the shafts drop.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 2.471 | loop |\n| `use` | 2.4 | once |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.8 | hold |\n","resolution":{"width":256,"height":256},"elements":[{"name":"floor","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-17.0,24.0,-48.0],"to":[17.0,26.0,48.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,14.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[160,167,194.0,169.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[129,162,225.0,164.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[194,167,228.0,169.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[0,165,96.0,167.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[0,0,34.0,96.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[34,0,68.0,96.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"660c0d05-2731-5048-8300-da5c26051f11"},{"name":"sill_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[15.5,20.5,-48.0],"to":[17.5,24.0,48.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,14.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[192,140,194.0,143.5],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[40,135,136.0,138.5],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[194,140,196.0,143.5],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[136,135,232.0,138.5],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[68,0,70.0,96.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[70,0,72.0,96.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"910c991d-e691-59a5-8057-c77391fc4717"},{"name":"side_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[15.5,26.0,-48.0],"to":[17.5,33.0,48.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,14.0,0.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[62,122,64.0,129.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[0,108,96.0,115.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[64,122,66.0,129.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[96,108,1